<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Aug retail trade sales up 3.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>S.African Aug retail trade sales up 3.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African retail trade sales rose a seasonally adjusted 3.2 percent month-on-month in August to 11.58 billion rand, latest Central Statistical Service (CSS) data shows.</p>
<p>Year-on-year, seasonally adjusted retail sales were up 13.4 percent from 10.21 billion rand in August 1995, the CSS said.</p>
<p>On an actual basis, retail trade sales were down 1.3 percent month-on-month and up 13.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Retail trade sales at current prices.</p>
<p>(rand million):</p>
<p>				 Aug '96	 Jul '96	Aug '95</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted  11,581.4	11,223.4     10,212.1</p>
<p>    Actual		   10,704.2	10,850.4	9,446.4</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
